; itempose.eval - a floor item's POSE and the click PICKS (code-review C180,
; C359, C258), read by tools\AllocTest.ps1 -Items.
;
; One pose (DungeonWorld::FloorItemPose) now answers where an item lies for the
; draw, its floor glow, a lit one's light and flame, and the pick; and every
; round click target is one ball test (Camera::Ray::HitsSphere). Each section
; below sets one thing up in an arena (`arena open 9 9`: floor 10,8..18,16) and
; reads it back:
;
;   --- niche open ---   a fire rune in an open wall niche: ONE glow row, and it
;                        stands over the rune in the pocket (the harness reads
;                        its `light at` against the rune's drawn middle from
;                        the niche pick below)
;   --- niche shut ---   the same niche shut: NO glow row (C180 - it glowed at
;                        the foot of the wall, giving a secret niche away)
;   --- niche pick ---   `pickprobe`: the rune is clicked at its drawn middle
;   --- floor pick ---   a torch and a rune side by side on the floor, each hit
;                        at five points across a quarter centred on its DRAWN
;                        box, at that box's middle height (C359 - the pick was
;                        measured at the model's height in model units, laid
;                        flat or not)
;   --- upright pick --- an upright potion and an iron key (a model-less item:
;                        the tablet, scaled up - picked at 0.45 m before, its
;                        drawn middle is a few centimetres), likewise
;   --- sconce pick ---  the wall torch ahead, clicked at its drawn middle
;   --- chain pick ---   a wooden door's chain, clicked at its drawn middle
;   --- pad pick ---     a stone door's pad, likewise
;
; The floor items lie in the FAR quarters of the square ahead, or alone: a
; taller item in the quarter in front of another rightly takes a click on that
; one's near edge (its column is in front), which is not what is measured here.
; Every `pickprobe` ends `pickprobe RESULT=PASS|FAIL|NONE` with counts by kind.
; The rune goes in with `niche ... put`: the editor's item brush cannot reach a
; niche until code-review C351 lands. One line runs per frame and `lights` reads
; the last frame's lights, so the echoes are the wait.
logecho on
reset
timescale 0
arena open 9 9
tp 14 9
face n
editor place wallfeatures niche 14 8 north
mappage close
niche 14 8 n put rune_fire
echo frame
echo frame
echo --- niche open ---
lights
niche 14 8 n shut
echo frame
echo frame
echo --- niche shut ---
lights
niche 14 8 n open
echo frame
echo frame
echo --- niche pick ---
pickprobe
tp 14 14
face n
editor place items torch 14 13
editor place items rune_fire 14 13
mappage close
echo frame
echo frame
echo --- floor pick ---
pickprobe
tp 11 14
face n
editor place items potion_health 11 13
editor place items iron_key 11 13
mappage close
echo frame
echo frame
echo --- upright pick ---
pickprobe
tp 12 8
face n
editor place fixtures sconce 12 8 north
mappage close
echo frame
echo frame
echo --- sconce pick ---
pickprobe
arena corridor 11
tp 14 12
face e
editor place doors wooden_door 15 12
mappage close
echo frame
echo frame
echo --- chain pick ---
pickprobe
editor erase 15 12
editor place doors stone_door 15 12
mappage close
echo frame
echo frame
echo --- pad pick ---
pickprobe
